                     <provenance type="#l"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_133">Chertsey, Surrey.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Peter</orgName><p>Distinctive entries (found also in
                        the Chertsey Breviary, i.e. <ref
                        target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_1669">Bodl., Lat.
                        liturg. e. 6</ref> etc) are: 7 May, octave of Erkenwald; 1 June, Simeon
                        confessor; 2 August Aethelwold confessor; 3 October the two (H)Ewalds. This
                        attribution was first recorded in the 1987 Supplement, on the basis of
                        information from Prof. R. W. Pfaff. In the 1987 Supplement, the shelfmark
                        was given as MS 252, but the corresponding MLGB index card indicates that
                        this attribution relates specifically to part II only.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_335">London. Augustinian
